# ── The two shared logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `memory.md` and `context.md` are one file each, shared by every session and
# every worktree. But a worktree is a separate checkout, so each one holds its
# own working copy, and the copies drift the moment two branches both append —
# which they do, because appending to memory.md is how a session signs off.
#
# `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides' lines instead of raising a conflict, which is
# the right semantics for an append-only log: nothing is lost and no session has
# to hand-resolve a diff it did not write.
#
# The cost, stated so it is not a surprise: union merge cannot know which entry
# came first, so after a merge the ordering near the top may interleave. Check
# it. Nothing is lost either way, which is the property that matters.
memory.md   merge=union
context.md  merge=union

# ── Line endings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This is a WSL2 checkout edited from both Linux and Windows tooling, and a
# single stray CRLF has already cost a merge: `memory.md` showed as modified in
# the main checkout purely because one line had been rewritten with \r\n, and
# git refused to fast-forward over it. Normalise text on the way in so an
# editor's line-ending default can never again read as a real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything genuinely binary must not be touched by that normalisation.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.pdf       binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.pptx      binary
*.apk       binary
*.mp4       binary
